    "updated_at": "2024-12-11T16:04:03Z",
    "body": "I think #9841 should be able to cover this case, by putting the submit button inside of the dialog, and making the forms button a \"fake\" submit button that actually opens the dialog:\n\n```html\n<form ...>\n<input ...>\n<!-- etc -->\n<button type=\"button\" commandfor=\"d\" command=\"show-modal\">Submit...</button>\n<dialog role=\"confirmation\" id=\"d\">\n  <p>Are you sure you want to submit/delete/modify X?</p>\n  <button type=\"button\" commandfor=\"d\" command=\"close\">Cancel</button>\n  <button type=\"submit\" value=\"confirm\">Confirm</button>\n</dialog>\n</form>\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
